From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] soc: qcom: describe Cliffs7 LLCC policy and resources

Translate the exact Cliffs7 policy to native LLCC use-case names.
Require the OEM bank/broadcast windows, four hardware banks and the v5
register family before configuration writes. Keep EDAC disabled until
its access and interrupt contract is qualified. No board activation.

Policy: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource uke-v-oss
5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd, drivers/soc/qcom/llcc-qcom.c.
DT: MiCode/kernel_devicetree uke-v-oss
94c84aeb9e517dbde546fc732033c184094c8e57, qcom/cliffs{,7}.dtsi.
Same-SoC policy: OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm7675
fc892483f1d61f245924681eb5abd563564d9cba; table matches the Uke policy.
Source/build checks do not establish cache hits, speed or lifecycle.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
